{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStop"},"metadata":{"title":"MXLStartStop","roleHeading":"Enumeration","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStop"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStartStop","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStartStopO"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The start-stop type is used for an attribute of musical elements that can either start or stop, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tuplets."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStop"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The values of start and stop refer to how an element appears in musical score order, not in MusicXML document"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. An element with a stop attribute may precede the corresponding element with a start attribute within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML document. This is particularly common in multi-staff music. For example, the stopping point for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tuplet may appear in staff 1 before the starting point for the tuplet appears in staff 2 later in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When multiple elements with the same tag are used within the same note, their order within the MusicXML"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document should match the musical score order."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"to